> a(x: u64, y: u64) = x*y
> b(x: u64, y: u64) = y*x
> equiv a b
a and b are equal on the domain of a (proved by algebra: both sides expand to one polynomial in x, y mod 2^64)
> c(x: i64, y: i64) = x*y
> d(x: i64, y: i64) = y*x
> equiv c d
c and d are equal on the domain of c (proved by algebra: both sides expand to one polynomial in x, y mod 2^64)
